Subject: [PATCH] round C1.6: launch switch closes the $39.90 connection
 (coming soon + 30-min booking)

Tao, 2026-09-11: release to planning.goaa.ai on C1 without changing
api.goaa.ai. That API only accepts the old login's order tokens, so after
the Clerk cutover a signed-in customer's purchase would fail at checkout.
At launch the paid connection is closed; the 30-minute booking stays.

- app/lib/paid-connection.ts: runtime, server-side switch
  GOAA_PAID_CONNECTION=open reopens; unset or anything else = closed.
  Not NEXT_PUBLIC_: flipping it needs an env change and a restart, no build.
- app/layout.tsx (dynamic): stamps <html data-goaa-paid="open|closed">.
- goaa-tokens.css: .goaa-paid-closed hidden by default; when closed,
  .goaa-paid-open-only hides and .goaa-paid-closed shows. A page without
  the stamp keeps today's behaviour. Pure CSS: no new client state, no
  hydration mismatch.
- ProfessionalHandoffCard: paid button and fee copy are open-only; a closed
  twin says the paid connection is opening soon and links to the 30-minute
  booking (never charges). "Continue with AI" unchanged.
- ProfessionalConnectBar: whole bar open-only.
- MatterProfessionalConnect: paid block open-only, booking twin when closed.
- app/connect-pass/layout.tsx (new, dynamic): when closed, renders a notice
  and never mounts the checkout page, so no order-API call can start even
  from a stale bookmark or saved sign-in return target.

Untouched: app/connect-pass/page.tsx, ChatComponent purchase handlers
(hash-protected by test-product-handoff), order-api, api.goaa.ai.

Test: scripts/test-paid-connection-gate.cjs (7) transpiles the real files
(switch semantics, layout stamp, CSS, card twin in en/zh, top bar, matter
block, /connect-pass closed vs open). product-handoff, brand-font,
portal-shell still pass. c2-clerk candidate-shape lists app/connect-pass/
layout.tsx as a new route while uncommitted; clean once committed.

